FORMAT dicom

%header

# ── Mark as de-identified ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DICOM PS 3.15 Annex E requires this tag to be set to YES
ADD PatientIdentityRemoved YES

# ── Patient identity ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Values are computed in dicom.py variable builders and injected via var:
REPLACE PatientID var:anon_patient_id
REPLACE PatientName var:anon_patient_name
REPLACE PatientBirthDate var:anon_birth_date
KEEP ReferringPhysicianName
BLANK OtherPatientIDs
BLANK AdditionalPatientHistory
BLANK Occupation
BLANK OtherPatientNames
BLANK MedicalRecordLocator

# ── Study / accession ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BLANK AccessionNumber # REPLACE AccessionNumber var:anon_accession_number # Use if there is a method for keeping salt confidential.

# ── Dates — jitter by var:date_jitter days ───────────────────────────────────
# date_jitter is an integer (days) set via DEID_DATE_JITTER env var (default 10)
# PatientBirthDate is handled by REPLACE above (year + 0101)
JITTER StudyDate var:date_jitter
JITTER SeriesDate var:date_jitter
JITTER AcquisitionDate var:date_jitter
JITTER ContentDate var:date_jitter
JITTER InstanceCreationDate var:date_jitter

# ── Times — zero out (preserve relative ordering within a study) ──────────────
BLANK PatientBirthTime

# ── Protocol / description (may contain free text PHI) ───────────────────────
# Comment these out if your downstream analysis needs protocol descriptions.
BLANK AdmittingDiagnosisDescription
BLANK OperatorName
BLANK PerformingPhysicianName
BLANK PhysicianOfRecord

# ── Comments ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PatientComments carries structured field mapping (Project/Subject/Session)
REPLACE PatientComments var:patient_comments
BLANK ImageComments
BLANK AdmissionID
BLANK AdmittingDiagnosesDescription
BLANK NameOfPhysicianReadingStudy
BLANK ReferringPhysicianAddress
BLANK ReferringPhysicianPhoneNumbers
